course: dictionary
lesson: 3851
title: Founder: a starter, a sinker, or a failure?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Look at the clues in the sentence before you decide. «Its founder is the person who started it» is about a business, so founder means the person who starts something.
explain: Now read «The ship began to founder in the storm.» A ship is a boat, and a storm is bad weather, so founder must be a verb about a ship. Swap in your meaning: "The ship began to fill with water and sink" makes sense, so that is the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes the clues point to a plan, not a ship. If a plan founders, it fails or comes to nothing. Ask yourself: what is the subject of the sentence? A person, a ship, a plan, or a horse? The subject tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Founder (noun) means a person who starts a school, company, club, charity or city.
fact: «Its founder is the person who started it» shows a founder is the one who began a business.
fact: Founder (verb) can mean that a ship fills with water and sinks.
fact: Founder (verb) can also mean that a plan fails or comes to nothing, or that a horse goes lame or stumbles.
fact: A co-founder is one of two or more people who start something together.
exercise: «The founders of the school met every Monday.» In this sentence, what is a founder? | The people who failed their exams | The people who sank the school bus | The people who painted the walls | * The people who started the school
exercise: «The company was started small, and its founder worked in a garage.» What does founder mean here? | A horse with sore feet | A ship that is sinking | A plan that has failed | * The person who began the company
exercise: «The boat began to founder in the storm.» What does founder mean? | Sail quickly across the bay | Paint its sides bright red | * Fill with water and sink | Turn around and head home
test: «The plan began to founder when the money ran out.» What does founder mean here? | Set off on a journey | Was painted gold | Grew bigger and better | * Failed and came to nothing
test: «Mia and Sam were co-founders of the club.» What does co-founder tell us? | A club member who joins later | * One of two people who started the club together | A person who closes a club | A club's favourite game
exam: Grandad says, «The horse began to founder on the hill.» What does founder mean? | Lie down and sleep | Eat all the grass | Sprint up the hill | * Go lame or stumble
